&lt;p&gt;ðŸ‘‰ &lt;a href="https://cashflow4375.gumroad.com/l/ujkqxb?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=article&amp;amp;utm_campaign=aps_first_sale&amp;amp;utm_content=schannel-event-36887-fatal-alert" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://cashflow4375.gumroad.com/l/ujkqxb?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=article&amp;amp;utm_campaign=aps_first_sale&amp;amp;utm_content=schannel-event-36887-fatal-alert&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;If you want the rest of the Intune runway written down for the team (enrollment hygiene, compliance phasing, break/fix cards and read-only PowerShell snapshots), the &lt;strong&gt;Intune &amp;amp; M365 Admin Starter Pack&lt;/strong&gt; pairs with this triage: &lt;a href="https://cashflow4375.gumroad.com/l/joonf?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=article&amp;amp;utm_campaign=aps_first_sale&amp;amp;utm_content=schannel-event-36887-fatal-alert" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://cashflow4375.gumroad.com/l/joonf?utm_source=devto&amp;amp;utm_medium=article&amp;amp;utm_campaign=aps_first_sale&amp;amp;utm_content=schannel-event-36887-fatal-alert&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Admin Pack Studio; not affiliated with Microsoft. Steps 1-8 and 10 are read-only checks: &lt;code&gt;Get-WinEvent&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Get-NetTCPConnection&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Get-Process&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Get-ComputerInfo&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Get-ChildItem&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;Get-ItemProperty&lt;/code&gt; on the SCHANNEL, Cryptography, .NET Framework, and WinHTTP registry keys, &lt;code&gt;Get-ItemPropertyValue&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Get-TlsCipherSuite&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;netsh http show sslcert&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;certutil -store&lt;/code&gt;, a &lt;code&gt;pktmon&lt;/code&gt; capture with &lt;code&gt;etl2pcap&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;Invoke-WebRequest -Method Head&lt;/code&gt;. Raising or restoring Schannel &lt;code&gt;EventLogging&lt;/code&gt;, enabling or disabling protocol versions under SCHANNEL\Protocols, setting the .NET &lt;code&gt;SystemDefaultTlsVersions&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;SchUseStrongCrypto&lt;/code&gt; values or the WinHTTP &lt;code&gt;DefaultSecureProtocols&lt;/code&gt; value, &lt;code&gt;Enable-TlsCipherSuite&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;Disable-TlsCipherSuite&lt;/code&gt;, the SSL Cipher Suite Order policy, and restarts are deliberate changes. Change one link at a time, prove it with the same peer after a reboot, and check current Microsoft Learn for version-specific behavior.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;By the end of this tutorial you will have a short Python script that pulls adverts from willhaben.at, the Austrian classifieds site, into structured rows: asking price, seller type, location, photo links and the advert's own address on the site.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Willhaben Scraper&lt;/strong&gt; (&lt;code&gt;reventadata/willhaben-scraper&lt;/code&gt;) is the Apify Actor built for this site. You give it one or more keywords, it walks the public search pages, and it returns one row per advert.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This guide runs it from Python with the Apify Python client. The sample rows below are copied from a real run of the Actor's example task on 18 November 2026, not from an invented example.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Prerequisites
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You need three things:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Python 3.11 or newer&lt;/strong&gt;, because the Apify client for Python 3.x requires it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A free &lt;strong&gt;Apify account&lt;/strong&gt;. You can sign up with an email address or a GitHub login.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your &lt;strong&gt;API token&lt;/strong&gt;, which belongs to your Apify account.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Install the client and export the token:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;pip install -U &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"apify-client~=3.0"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="kd"&gt;export&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nv"&gt;APIFY_API_TOKEN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"your_apify_token_here"&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;No scraping code is needed on your side. The Actor reads the public pages, so you do not need a login on willhaben.at.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  What you'll achieve
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You will search willhaben.at for the keyword &lt;code&gt;iphone&lt;/code&gt;, read the rows in Python and print one line per advert: the price as the site shows it, the town, and whether the seller is private or a business.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same input works for a buyer comparing asking prices, a seller checking what similar adverts ask, or an analyst building a table by Austrian federal state. Only the input changes. Every section of willhaben.at returns the same columns, so the script stays the same when you switch to real estate or cars.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 1: Open Willhaben Scraper
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open the &lt;a href="https://apify.com/reventadata/willhaben-scraper" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;Willhaben Scraper page on Apify Store&lt;/a&gt;. The &lt;strong&gt;Try for free&lt;/strong&gt; button there opens the Actor in Apify Console. This guide uses the Python client, so you only need the Actor name, &lt;code&gt;reventadata/willhaben-scraper&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 2: Choose the search
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The search is described by a few input fields:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;vertical&lt;/code&gt;: the section of willhaben.at. &lt;code&gt;marketplace&lt;/code&gt; (Marktplatz, the general classifieds and the default), &lt;code&gt;realEstate&lt;/code&gt; (Immobilien) or &lt;code&gt;cars&lt;/code&gt; (Gebrauchtwagen).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;searchQueries&lt;/code&gt;: keywords, one per line. Marktplatz only. Each keyword is searched separately, and an advert that two keywords both find is pushed once.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;searchPath&lt;/code&gt;: an optional category or region page, copied from the address bar of willhaben.at. It must start with the section's own path, for example &lt;code&gt;immobilien/mietwohnungen/wien&lt;/code&gt;. A path that carries a &lt;code&gt;?&lt;/code&gt; filter fails the run, and the run's message says to put keywords in &lt;code&gt;searchQueries&lt;/code&gt; instead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;maxItems&lt;/code&gt;: a hard cap on rows across all keywords. The schema default is 100.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;maxPagesPerSearch&lt;/code&gt;: an optional cap on result pages for each keyword. Each page holds 100 adverts, and the site stops at 999 pages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The example task of this run sends exactly this input:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight json"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"searchQueries"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"iphone"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"vertical"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"marketplace"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"maxItems"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="nl"&gt;"maxPagesPerSearch"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Read it as: one keyword, the marketplace section, at most ten rows, and at most one results page for that keyword.&lt;/p&gt;




&lt;h2&gt;


  Step 3: Run it from Python
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This script starts the Actor, waits for it, reads the dataset and prints one line per advert:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight python"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;from&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;apify_client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;import&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ApifyClient&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 1. Initialise the client with your token from the environment&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;ApifyClient&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;os&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;environ&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"APIFY_API_TOKEN"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 2. Describe the search: the same input as the example task&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;run_input&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"searchQueries"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"iphone"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"vertical"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"marketplace"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"maxItems"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"maxPagesPerSearch"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="mi"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 3. Start the Actor and wait for it to finish&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;actor&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"reventadata/willhaben-scraper"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;call&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run_input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run_input&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;is&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;None&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="ow"&gt;or&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;!=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"SUCCEEDED"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;status&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;if&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;else&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"unknown"&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;raise&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nc"&gt;SystemExit&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Run did not succeed (status: {status})."&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 4. Read the rows from the run's default dataset&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="n"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;client&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;dataset&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;default_dataset_id&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;list_items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"Retrieved {len(items)} adverts.\n"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;

&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# 5. Print one line per advert: price as shown, town, seller type, link&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="k"&gt;for&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="k"&gt;in&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="n"&gt;items&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="n"&gt;seller&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;{&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="kc"&gt;True&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"private"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="kc"&gt;False&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;:&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"business"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;item&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nf"&gt;get&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"isPrivateSeller"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;,&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="s2"&gt;"not stated"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"{item.get('priceDisplay')}  {item.get('location')}  {seller}"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
    &lt;span class="k"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="n"&gt;f&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="s2"&gt;"  {item.get('url')}"&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;)&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;The output starts like this. The first two of the ten lines are shown:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
