&lt;h2&gt;


  Understanding your results
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The rows have one fixed set of columns. The ones you will use most:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;price&lt;/code&gt; (a number) and &lt;code&gt;priceDisplay&lt;/code&gt; (the text as the site shows it, for example &lt;code&gt;"€ 1.389"&lt;/code&gt;). &lt;code&gt;currency&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;EUR&lt;/code&gt; when the displayed price starts with the euro sign.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;oldPrice&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;priceReducedAt&lt;/code&gt;: the previous price and the date when the seller lowered it. Three of the ten rows carry both.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;isPrivateSeller&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; for a private seller, &lt;code&gt;false&lt;/code&gt; for a business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;sellerName&lt;/code&gt;: the business name. Six rows have it, and the four private rows have it empty.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;location&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;postcode&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;state&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;district&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;latitude&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;longitude&lt;/code&gt;. All ten rows have coordinates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;title&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;description&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;url&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;publishedAt&lt;/code&gt;. The &lt;code&gt;description&lt;/code&gt; is the start of the advert text as the search list shows it, ending in &lt;code&gt;...&lt;/code&gt; when the site shortens it. In this run seven of the ten descriptions are shortened, at 252 to 257 characters. The other three run 16 to 38 characters and are not shortened.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;imageUrl&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;imageUrls&lt;/code&gt; and &lt;code&gt;imageCount&lt;/code&gt;. The rows hold one to five photos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;code&gt;isBumped&lt;/code&gt;: &lt;code&gt;true&lt;/code&gt; on six of the ten rows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

